    q: "What macro tools are included?",
    a: "A market stress meter, VIX gauge with term-structure regime detection, the Fear & Greed index, a live yield curve with inversion history, sector rotation quadrants (RRG), a cross-asset correlation matrix, a historical crisis playbook, a live US debt clock, a high-impact economic calendar, and AI-written macro briefings.",
  },
  {
    q: "Is FinBrio free?",
    a: "The core app is free: live markets across 46 indices, 23 commodities and 44 forex pairs, the market-cap heatmap, S1–S3 AI signals, the Power Moves scanner, smart-money tracking, tariff exposure, multibaggers, the ETF explorer, and the full macro dashboard. A single Pro subscription unlocks advanced strategies, unlimited alerts, AI analyst notes and macro briefings, AI-powered tariff analysis, extended timeframes, and advanced backtest filtering.",
  },
  {
    q: "Where does the data come from?",
    a: "Market data comes from Yahoo Finance; hedge-fund positioning from the CFTC's Disaggregated COT report; the debt clock from the US Treasury's FiscalData API; tariff data from USTR Section 301 schedules; presidential (OGE Form 278-T), insider (SEC EDGAR) and lobbying (US Senate LDA) disclosures from official public sources; and country statistics from the World Bank.",
  },
  {
    q: "Is FinBrio financial advice?",
    a: "No. FinBrio is an information and analytics tool. Signals, backtests, and briefings are for informational purposes only and are not investment advice. Markets involve risk — always do your own research.",
